\mt1 1 Thessalonians
\c 1
\s1 Greetings to the Thessalonians
\r (\ref 2 Thessalonians 1:1–4|2TH 1:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 1 Paul, Silvanus,\f + \fr 1:1 \ft That is, Silas\f* and Timothy,
\p To the church of the Thessalonians in God \add the\add* Father and \add the\add* Lord Jesus Christ:
\p Grace and peace to you.\f + \fr 1:1 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ\ft .\f*
\p \v 2 We always thank God for all of you, remembering \add you\add* in our prayers \v 3 \add and\add* continually recalling before our God and Father your work of faith, \add your\add* labor of love, and \add your\add* enduring hope in our Lord Jesus Christ.
\p \v 4 Brothers who are beloved by God, we know \add that\add* He has chosen you, \v 5 because our gospel came to you not only in word, but also in power, in \add the\add* Holy Spirit, and with great conviction — just as you know we lived among you for your sake. \v 6 And you became imitators of us and of the Lord when you welcomed the message with \add the\add* joy of \add the\add* Holy Spirit, in \add spite of your\add* great suffering.
\p \v 7 As a result, you have become an example to all the believers in Macedonia and Achaia. \v 8 For not only \add did\add* the message of the Lord ring out from you to Macedonia and Achaia, but your faith in God has gone out to every place, so that we have no need to say anything \add more\add*. \v 9 For they themselves report what kind of welcome you gave us, and how you turned to God from idols to serve \add the\add* living and true God \v 10 and to await His Son from heaven, whom He raised from the dead — Jesus our deliverer from the coming wrath.
\c 2
\s1 Paul’s Ministry
\p \v 1 You yourselves know, brothers, that our visit to you was not in vain. \v 2 As you are aware, we had already endured suffering and shameful treatment in Philippi. But in the face of strong opposition, we were bold in our God to speak to you the gospel of God.
\p \v 3 For our appeal does not arise from deceit \add or\add* ulterior motives \add or\add* trickery. \v 4 Instead, we speak as those approved by God to be entrusted with the gospel, not in order to please men but God, who examines our hearts. \v 5 As you know, we never used words of flattery \add or any\add* pretext for greed. God \add is our\add* witness! \v 6 Nor did we seek praise from you \add or\add* from anyone else, \add although\add* as apostles of Christ we had authority to demand \add it\add*.\f + \fr 2:6 \ft Or \fqa although as apostles of Christ we could have been a burden to you\ft ; SBL, NE, and WH include this phrase with verse 7.\f*
\p \v 7 On the contrary, we were gentle among you,\f + \fr 2:7 \ft WH and NA \fqa we were like young children among you\f* like a nursing mother caring for her children. \v 8 We cared so deeply \add that\add* we were delighted to share with you not only the gospel of God, but our own lives as well. That is how beloved you have become to us.
\p \v 9 Surely you recall, brothers, our labor and toil. We worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to anyone while we proclaimed to you the gospel of God. \v 10 You \add are\add* witnesses, and \add so is\add* God, of how holy, righteous, and blameless our conduct was among you who believed. \v 11 For you know that \add we treated\add* each of you as a father \add treats\add* his own children— \v 12 encouraging \add you\add*, comforting you, and urging you to walk in a manner worthy of God, who calls you into His own kingdom and glory.
\p \v 13 And we continually thank God because, when you received \add the\add* word of God that you heard from us, you accepted \add it\add* not \add as the\add* word of men, but as it truly is, \add the\add* word of God, which is also \add now\add* at work in you who believe.
\p \v 14 For you, brothers, became imitators of the churches of God in Judea that are in Christ Jesus. You suffered from \add your\add* own countrymen the very things they \add suffered\add* from the Jews, \v 15 who killed both the Lord Jesus and their own prophets and drove us out \add as well\add*. They are displeasing to God and hostile to all men, \v 16 hindering us from telling the Gentiles how they may be saved. As a result, \add they\add* continue to heap up their sins \add to full capacity\add*; the utmost wrath has come upon them.\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Or \fqa at last the wrath (of God) has come upon them.\f*
\s1 Paul’s Longing to Visit
\p \v 17 Brothers, although we were torn away from you for a short time (in person, not in heart), \add our\add* desire to see you face \add to face\add* was even more intense. \v 18 For we wanted to come to you — indeed I, Paul, \add tried\add* again and again — but Satan obstructed us. \v 19 After all, who \add is\add* our hope, \add our\add* joy, \add our\add* crown of boasting, if it is not you yourselves in the presence of our Lord Jesus at His coming? \v 20 You are indeed our glory and \add our\add* joy.
\c 3
\s1 Timothy’s Visit
\p \v 1 So \add when\add* we could bear \add it\add* no longer, we were willing to be left on our own in Athens. \v 2 We sent Timothy, our brother and fellow worker for God\f + \fr 3:2 \ft Or \fqa our brother and God’s fellow worker\ft ; NE, WH, BYZ, and TR \fqa our brother and minister of God\f* in the gospel of Christ, to strengthen and encourage you in your faith, \v 3 so that none \add of you\add* would be shaken by these trials. For you know that we are destined for this. \v 4 Indeed, when we were with you, we kept warning you that we would suffer persecution; and as you know, it has come to pass. \v 5 For this reason, \add when\add* I could bear \add it\add* no longer, I sent to find out about your faith, \add for fear that\add* the tempter \add had\add* somehow tempted you and that our labor might have been in vain.
\s1 Timothy’s Encouraging Report
\p \v 6 But just now, Timothy has returned from  \add his visit\add* with the good news about your faith, \add your\add* love, and \add the\add* fond memories you have preserved, longing to see us just as we \add long to see\add* you. \v 7 For this reason, brothers, in all our distress and persecution, we have been reassured about you, because of your faith. \v 8 For now we can go on living, as long as you are standing firm in \add the\add* Lord.
\p \v 9 How can we \add adequately\add* thank God for you in return for our great joy over you in \add His\add* presence? \v 10 Night and day we pray most earnestly that we may see you face to face and supply what is lacking in your faith.
\p \v 11 Now \add may\add* our God and Father Himself, and our Lord Jesus, direct our way to you. \v 12 And \add may\add* the Lord cause you to increase and overflow with love for one another and for everyone \add else\add*, just as our \add love\add* for you \add overflows\add*, \v 13 so that He may establish your hearts in blamelessness \add and\add* holiness before our God and Father at the coming of our Lord Jesus with all His saints. Amen.
\c 4
\s1 Living to Please God
\p \v 1 Finally, brothers, we ask and encourage you in \add the\add* Lord Jesus to live in a way that is pleasing to God, just as you have received from us. This is how you already live, so you should do so all the more. \v 2 For you know \add the\add* instructions we gave you by the authority of the Lord Jesus.
\p \v 3 For it is God’s will that you should be holy: You must abstain from sexual immorality; \v 4 each of you must know \add how\add* to control his \add own\add* body\f + \fr 4:4 \ft Literally \fqa know how to possess his own vessel\f* in holiness and honor, \v 5 not in lustful passion like the Gentiles who do not know God; \v 6 \add and\add* no one should \add ever\add* violate \add or\add* exploit his brother in \add this\add* regard,\f + \fr 4:6 \ft Or \fqa no one should ever harm or cheat his brother in this matter\f* because \add the\add* Lord will avenge all such \add acts\add*, as we have already told you and solemnly warned \add you\add*. \v 7 For God \add has\add* not called us to impurity, but to holiness. \v 8 Anyone, then, who rejects \add this command does\add* not reject man but God, the very \add One who\add* gives you His Holy Spirit.
\p \v 9 Now about brotherly love, you do not need \add anyone\add* to write to you, because you yourselves have been taught by God to love one another. \v 10 And you are indeed showing this \add love\add* to all the brothers throughout Macedonia. But we urge you, brothers, to excel more and more \v 11 and to aspire to live quietly, to attend to your own \add matters\add*, and to work with your own hands, as we instructed you. \v 12 Then you will behave properly toward outsiders, \add without\add* being dependent \add on anyone\add*.
\s1 The Return of the Lord
\p \v 13 Brothers, we do not want you to be uninformed about those who sleep  \add in death \add*,\f + \fr 4:13 \ft Literally \fqa those who have fallen asleep\ft , as in verses 14 and 15\f* so that you will not grieve like the rest, who are without hope. \v 14 For since we believe that Jesus died and rose again, we also believe that God will bring with \add Jesus\add* those who have fallen asleep in \add Him\add*.
\p \v 15 By \add the\add* word of \add the\add* Lord, we declare to you that we who are alive \add and\add* remain until the coming of the Lord will by no means precede those who have fallen asleep. \v 16 For the Lord Himself will descend from heaven with a loud command, with the voice of an archangel, and with \add the\add* trumpet of God, and the dead in Christ will be the first to rise. \v 17 After that, we who are alive \add and\add* remain will be caught up together with them in \add the\add* clouds to meet the Lord in \add the\add* air. And so we will always \add be\add* with \add the\add* Lord.
\p \v 18 Therefore encourage one another with these words.
\c 5
\s1 The Day of the Lord
\r (\ref Zephaniah 1:7–18|ZEP 1:7-18\ref*; \ref Malachi 4:1–6|MAL 4:1-6\ref*; \ref 2 Peter 3:8–13|2PE 3:8-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 Now about the times and seasons, brothers, \add we do\add* not need to write to you. \v 2 For you \add are\add* fully aware that \add the\add* Day of \add the\add* Lord will come like a thief in \add the\add* night. \v 3 While \add people\add* are saying, “Peace and security,” destruction will come upon them suddenly, like labor pains on a pregnant woman, and they will not escape.
\p \v 4 But you, brothers, are not in \add the\add* darkness so that \add this\add* day should overtake you like a thief. \v 5 For you are all sons of \add the\add* light and sons of \add the\add* day; we do not belong to \add the\add* night \add or\add* to \add the\add* darkness. \v 6 So then, let us not sleep as the others \add do\add*, but let us remain awake and sober. \v 7 For those who sleep, sleep at night, and those who get drunk, get drunk at night. \v 8 But \add since\add* we belong to \add the\add* day, let us be sober, putting on \add the\add* breastplate of faith and love, and \add the\add* helmet \add of our\add* hope of salvation.
\p \v 9 For God has not appointed us to \add suffer\add* wrath, but to obtain salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ. \v 10 He died for us so that, whether we are awake or asleep, we may live together with Him. \v 11 Therefore encourage and build one another \add up\add*, just as you are already doing.
\s1 Christian Living
\p \v 12 But we ask you, brothers, to acknowledge those who work diligently among you, \add who\add* care for you in \add the\add* Lord and \add who\add* admonish you. \v 13 In love, hold them in highest \add regard\add* because of their work. Live in peace with one another.
\p \v 14 And we urge you, brothers, to admonish the unruly, encourage the fainthearted, help the weak, \add and\add* be patient with everyone.
\p \v 15 Make sure that no one repays evil for evil. Always pursue what \add is\add* good for one another and for all \add people\add*.
\p \v 16 Rejoice at all times. \v 17 Pray without ceasing. \v 18 Give thanks in every circumstance, for this \add is\add* God’s will for you in Christ Jesus.
\p \v 19 Do not extinguish the Spirit. \v 20 Do not treat prophecies \add with contempt\add*, \v 21 but test all things. Hold fast to what \add is\add* good. \v 22 Abstain from every form of evil.
\s1 Final Blessings and Instructions
\p \v 23 Now \add may\add* the God of peace Himself sanctify you completely, and \add may\add* your entire spirit, soul, and body be kept blameless\f + \fr 5:23 \ft Or \fqa may your spirit, soul, and body be kept entirely blameless\f* at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ. \v 24 The \add One who\add* calls you \add is\add* faithful, and \add He\add* will do \add it\add*.
\p \v 25 Brothers, pray for us as well.
\p \v 26 Greet all the brothers with a holy kiss.
\p \v 27 I charge you \add before\add* the Lord \add to have this\add* letter read to all the brothers.
\p \v 28 The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ \add be\add* with you.\f + \fr 5:28 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa Amen.\f*
